 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489076 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489076 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489076 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "72ae3726-b8b0-5976-82de-d20849cd73be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488842 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489080 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7599f77d-da1f-5c75-baeb-b3ad971719bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488722 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489117 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b4d356cb-97ed-53b6-8ae4-08e38186803d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488737 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489143 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d99aa76c-d573-53bf-9199-ad883ba2b9fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489146 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186488489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489146 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489146 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489146 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186488489 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489146 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dd35897b-af9b-538f-9da8-73a25cda3699" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489182 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489076 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489182 #edb/ref 1069 "q-67262" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489182 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489182 #edb/ref 1071 "The formula to calculate the distance that an object in uniform rectilinear motion has traveled is given by\n\n$$\nd=v\\cdot t,\n$$\n\nwhere $v$ represents the velocity of the moving object and $t$ represents time.\n\nWhat is the formula for velocity in terms of distance and time?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489182 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "14cd0a28-442e-5455-9aaf-cc966e4aa8e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489182 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $v,$ so we will treat the other variables $d$ and $t$ as constants. Since $v$ is being multiplied by $t,$ we need to divide both sides of the equation by $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =v\\cdot t \\\\ \\frac{d}{t} & =\\frac{v\\cdot t}{t} \\\\ \\frac{d}{t} & =\\frac{v\\cdot \\cancel{t}}{\\cancel{t}} \\\\ \\frac{d}{t} & =v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $v=\\frac{d}{t}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $t\\ne 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489183 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489143 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489183 #edb/ref 1069 "q-6272" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489183 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489183 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve for $a$ where $c=3a+7b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489183 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "16ef2d7f-f052-5e96-9861-83b3cce4c0bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489183 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $a,$ so we will treat the other variables $b$ and $c$ constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $a.$\n\nFirst, we subtract $7b$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =3a+7b \\\\ c-7b & =3a+7b-7b \\\\ c-7b & =3a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3a & =c-7b \\\\ \\frac{3a}{3} & =\\frac{c-7b}{3} \\\\ a & =\\frac{c-7b}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489189 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489080 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489189 #edb/ref 1069 "q-44850" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489189 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489189 #edb/ref 1071 "In business, the economic profit is defined as\n\n$$\nE=PQ-C,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ is the sale price of a good, $Q$ is the number of goods sold, and $C$ is the cost of producing $Q$ goods. \n\nWhat is the formula for the price in terms of the other variables?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489189 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "220b7284-89df-58d8-b7fb-14c6a632a4f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489189 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $P,$ so we will treat the other variables $E,$ $Q,$ and $C$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $P.$\n\nFirst, we add $C$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E & =PQ-C \\\\ E+C & =PQ-C+C \\\\ E+C & =PQ\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $Q$ to get $P$ alone:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E+C & =PQ \\\\ \\frac{E+C}{Q} & =\\frac{PQ}{Q} \\\\ \\frac{E+C}{Q} & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $P=\\frac{E+C}{Q}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $Q\\ne 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489192 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489070 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489192 #edb/ref 1069 "q-75547" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489192 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489192 #edb/ref 1071 "The surface area of a cylinder is given by \n\n$$\nA=2\\pi rh\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the radius and $h$ is the height of the cylinder.\n\nWhat is the formula for the height of the cylinder in terms of the other variables?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489192 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "237b013e-fcd6-5777-9bce-b39ac50c9f8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489192 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $h,$ so we will treat the other variables $A$ and $r$ as constants.\n\nFirst, we rearrange and then divide both sides by $2\\pi r$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =2\\pi rh \\\\ A & =(2\\pi r)h \\\\ \\frac{A}{2\\pi r} & =\\frac{(2\\pi r)h}{2\\pi r} \\\\ \\frac{A}{2\\pi r} & =h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $h=\\frac{A}{2\\pi r}.$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that $r\\ne 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489233 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489233 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215068" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489233 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489233 #edb/ref 1071 "If $y=5w+7x,$ then $x=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489233 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ab827a9-09e7-59f8-93b4-f0c91318eeaa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489233 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $x,$ so we will treat the other variables $w$ and $y$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $x.$\n\nFirst, we subtract $5w$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5w+7x \\\\ y-5w & =5w+7x-5w \\\\ y-5w & =7x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $7:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x & =y-5w \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & =\\frac{y-5w}{7} \\\\ x & =\\frac{y-5w}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489239 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489117 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489239 #edb/ref 1069 "q-104505" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489239 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489239 #edb/ref 1071 "Make $k$ the subject of the equation $-2h=2m-3k.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489239 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8670623f-a7f4-578e-914d-6583efa2a94c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489239 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $k,$ so we will treat the other variables $h$ and $m$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $k.$\n\nFirst, we add $3k$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2h & =2m-3k \\\\ -2h+3k & =2m-3k+3k \\\\ 3k-2h & =2m\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we add $2h$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k-2h & =2m \\\\ 3k-2h+2h & =2m+2h \\\\ 3k & =2m+2h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3k & =2m+2h \\\\ \\frac{3k}{3} & =\\frac{2m+2h}{3} \\\\ k & =\\frac{2(m+h)}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489276 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489276 #edb/ref 1069 "q-215396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489276 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489276 #edb/ref 1071 "If $2xz-3y=4w,$ then $y=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489276 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de5d5814-9f69-514d-a764-4ee1edcf544a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186489276 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to isolate $y,$ so we will treat the other variables $w,x,$ and $z$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $y.$\n\nFirst, we subtract $2xz$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2xz-3y & =4w \\\\ 2xz-3y-2xz & =4w-2xz \\\\ -3y & =4w-2xz\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide by $-3$ to get $y$ alone:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y & =4w-2xz \\\\ \\frac{-3y}{-3} & =\\frac{4w-2xz}{-3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{4w-2xz}{-3} \\\\ y & =\\frac{2xz-4w}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
